            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did svasti mean, and what were its two pieces?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कृपया",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कृपया (kṛpayā) — \"please\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कृपया (kṛpayā) is please, and like most polite words in most languages it is not really a word for \"please\" at all. It is the noun kṛpā, \"compassion, kindness\", put into the case that means by means of. You are saying by your kindness."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English does the same thing and hides it just as well: please was once if it please you. Two languages, two buried sentences, one small polite noise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A polite word with a whole clause folded inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
