          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपकारः (upakāraḥ) — \"a favour, a good turn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपकारः (upakāraḥ) is a favour — something done for someone. Take it apart: upa, \"near, toward\", plus kāra, \"a doing\", from the root behind करोमि, \"I do\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So a favour is a doing-toward. And you have already seen kāra once, in नमस्कारः, \"the making of a bow\" — the same piece, in a word you have said since the first chapter. Prefixes and pieces are how Sanskrit builds, and by now you can watch it happen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
