          "title": "You'll want to know: धन्यः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धन्यः (dhanyaḥ) — \"fortunate, blessed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धन्यः (dhanyaḥ) means fortunate, blessed, rich in what matters. It is built on dhana, wealth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And it closes a circle. The very first thank-you in this book was धन्यवादः — and that word is dhanya + vāda, a saying of \"you are fortunate\". Sanskrit does not thank you by reporting your gift; it thanks you by calling you lucky. You said the word on the first day and could not see inside it. You can now."
            }
          ]
        },
